scxjnz.jpg"}, {"id": 1565136, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scxjo0.jpg"}, {"id": 1565137, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scxjo1.jpg"}, {"id": 1565138, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scxjo2.jpg"}, {"id": 1565140, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scxjo4.jpg"}, {"id": 1565139, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scxjo3.jpg"}, {"id": 1565141, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scxjo5.jpg"}, {"id": 1565142, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scxjo6.jpg"}], "slug": "truxton-ii", "storyline": "\u201cDuring the time of the grand battle known as Tatsujin, another battle was being fought in a remote area of the infinite universe, with similar stakes. The battle was known as Tatsujin Oh.\u201d", "summary": "Gameplay is similar to the previous Truxton. Truxton II has six huge areas, each with a boss at the end; the game \"loops\" these six areas forever. Lives are given out at 70000 points, then every 200000 points after; players start with three.\n\nThere are power-ups to increase ship speed, add a smartbomb to your stock, and change/strengthen your current weapon: red fires bombs in a small area around your ship, similar to the red weapon from Robo Aleste; blue is a homing laser, similar to the blue weapon from the original Truxton; while green fires wide-reaching salvos of green shots and more or less replaces the red weapon from Truxton.", "themes": [{"id": 18, "name": "Science fiction"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/truxton-ii", "videos": [{"id": 153867, "name": "Gameplay Video", "video_id": "W5TPLmA9nM4", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W5TPLmA9nM4", "title": "Truxton II. [Arcade - Toaplan}.  (1992).  1CC. No Death - 1LOOP. 60Fps.", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/W5TPLmA9nM4/maxresdefault.jpg"}], "collections": [{"id": 3589, "name": "Truxton"}]}